  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "A circle with radius \\(r\\) is contained within the region bounded by a circle with radius \\(R.\\) The area bounded by the larger circle is \\(\\frac{a}{b}\\) times the area of the region outside the smaller circle and inside the larger circle. Then \\(R:r\\) equals:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\sqrt a:\\sqrt b\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\sqrt a:\\sqrt{a-b}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\sqrt b:\\sqrt{a-b}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(a:\\sqrt{a-b}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(b:\\sqrt{a-b}\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1969-p13.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The area condition is \\[ \\pi R^2=\\frac ab\\pi(R^2-r^2). \\] Thus \\(bR^2=aR^2-ar^2,\\) so \\(ar^2=(a-b)R^2.\\) Therefore \\[ \\frac Rr=\\sqrt{\\frac a{a-b}}, \\] and \\(R:r=\\sqrt a:\\sqrt{a-b}.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Write \\(\\pi R^2=(\\frac{a}{b})\\pi(R^2-r^2)\\)",
        "Solve for the ratio \\(\\frac{R^2}{r^2}\\) before taking square roots"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
